    "body": "## Description\n\n`get_env_vars()` parsed its `additional_env_vars` string with `dict(item.split(\"=\") for item in s.split(\",\"))`, and the local scheduler builds that string by joining `scheduling.env_vars` as `k=v,k=v`. Any value containing `,` or `=` therefore raised `ValueError` when creating local workers. Examples: `PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF=expandable_segments:True,max_split_size_mb:128`, or `X=a=b`.\n\n- `get_env_vars` now also accepts a mapping, whose values are used verbatim.\n- The string form splits each item on the first `=` only (backward compatible).\n- `LocalScheduler` passes `scheduling.env_vars` directly instead of round-tripping through a string.\n- The slurm and ray schedulers call `get_env_vars()` without arguments and are unaffected.\n\n## Related Issue\n\nNo existing issue; I found no open or closed PR touching this (`gh pr list --search env_vars`).\n\n## Type of Change\n\n- [x] 🐛 Bug fix\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] I have read the [Contributing Guide](https://github.com/areal-project/community/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md) (commit is DCO signed off)\n- [ ] Pre-commit hooks pass (`pre-commit run --all-files`): not run; I ran `ruff format` and `ruff check` on the touched files only\n- [x] Relevant tests pass; new tests added: `tests/infra/test_launcher_utils.py` and `tests/infra/test_local_launcher.py` pass (9 passed). The two new env-var tests fail without the fix.\n- [ ] Self-reviewed via `/review-pr` command: not run\n- [ ] This PR was created by a coding agent via `/create-pr`: written with Claude Code, but without that command\n\n## Additional Context\n\nNot verified: the real `LocalScheduler.create_workers` path with GPUs; only `get_env_vars` and its unit tests were run (CPU, Python 3.12).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
